WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
Imagine you're organizing a picnic. Your team left

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.940
you a list of reminders to tidy up.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.910
The first says, setup at nine, bring folding

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.880
chairs. You want the reminders to sound friendly.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.086
In your team chat, ask the AI to

00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:17.733
rewrite the first reminder only. Say, make it

00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:20.379
friendly, keep the details, and stop there so

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:23.026
I can read it. Now you can see

00:00:23.026 --> 00:00:24.680
what it thinks friendly means.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.120
Here's a possible reply: Come help us set

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.000
up at nine! Sounds friendly. But imagine you're

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.880
the volunteer walking out the door. What were

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.760
you supposed to take with you? The folding

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.120
chairs.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.549
Reply in the same chat: keep the chairs,

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:43.419
and try that one again. Now it says,

00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:46.288
Join us at nine for setup. Please bring

00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:49.157
folding chairs! Read it back. Time, task, and

00:00:49.157 --> 00:00:50.592
chairs are all there.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.625
Now tell the AI to use that style

00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:56.089
for the rest and keep what to bring

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.554
in every reminder. Give the finished list a

00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:01.019
read before sending it. One quick check up

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:03.484
front saved you from fixing the same mistake

00:01:03.484 --> 00:01:04.408
in every line.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.408
Next time a job comes with a whole

00:01:07.408 --> 00:01:09.856
list, try saying these words: show me the

00:01:09.856 --> 00:01:12.304
first one, then wait. You can bring that

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.752
habit to whatever you ask AI to help

00:01:14.752 --> 00:01:17.200
with next. See you in the next tip.
